config PCOPY
	tristate "Parallel Copy/Move — NVMe Multi-Queue & PCIe Lane Aware"
	depends on BLOCK && BLK_DEV
	select PROC_FS
	help
	  PCOPY provides hardware-aware parallel file copy and move operations.
	  It detects NVMe hardware queue depth, PCIe lane width, and CPU count
	  to compute the optimal number of parallel I/O channels.

	  Standard cp/mv operates sequentially. PCOPY dispatches multiple files
	  across multiple channels simultaneously, each hitting a distinct NVMe
	  submission queue via blk-mq's per-CPU mapping. This saturates the
	  device's PCIe bandwidth when copying many files.

	  Channel count = min(online_cpus, hw_queues, nr_files)

	  Example: 8 CPUs + NVMe with 8 hw queues + 100 files = 8 channels
	  Each channel processes files in parallel, each on its own NVMe SQ.
	  PCIe Gen4 x4 = ~7 GB/s theoretical bandwidth, achievable with
	  sufficient queue depth.

	  Exposes:
	    /proc/pmove/status  - Hardware detection and recommendations
	    /proc/pmove/config  - Tunable parameters
	    /dev/pmove          - ioctl interface for pcopy/pmove tools

	  To compile as a module, choose M here: the module will be called pcopy.

	  If unsure, say M.
